WasmFS: open() with O_NOCTTY trips doOpen()'s flag assertion

musl's openpty() opens /dev/ptmx with O_NOCTTY, which aborted builds
with assertions instead of failing. O_NOCTTY means nothing to WasmFS.

Upstream: not filed yet
Draft: docs/upstream/emscripten-wasmfs-open-noctty.md

diff --git a/system/lib/wasmfs/syscalls.cpp b/system/lib/wasmfs/syscalls.cpp
index 55f6a00..d0a600a 100644
--- a/system/lib/wasmfs/syscalls.cpp
+++ b/system/lib/wasmfs/syscalls.cpp
@@ -438,7 +438,7 @@ static __wasi_fd_t doOpen(path::ParsedParent parsed,
   // TODO: remove assert when all functionality is complete.
   assert((flags & ~(O_CREAT | O_EXCL | O_DIRECTORY | O_TRUNC | O_APPEND |
                     O_RDWR | O_WRONLY | O_RDONLY | O_LARGEFILE | O_NOFOLLOW |
-                    O_CLOEXEC | O_NONBLOCK)) == 0);
+                    O_CLOEXEC | O_NONBLOCK | O_NOCTTY)) == 0);
 
   if (auto err = parsed.getError()) {
     return err;
